From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Velez Garcia <velezgarciaemmanuel25@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:14:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Arrow knockback follows the arrow, and align ADVANCED with
 reference behaviour

Vanilla derives arrow knockback from where the shooter is standing when
the arrow lands, not from the arrow's path. A shooter who strafes after
firing knocks the victim sideways, and an arrow shot at yourself picks a
random direction because shooter and victim share a position. Arrow
knockback now runs in EntityArrow along the arrow's own velocity, with bow
boosting using the shooter's yaw at the time of firing.

The ADVANCED model also moves to EntityHuman#attack, where the attacker's
facing and sprint state are available, and now matches the reference
implementation:

- knockback is sent along the attacker's facing and set outright rather
  than added to the victim's motion
- the 1.7 chase case triggers when both players face the same way and the
  victim is sprinting, instead of a positional back-hit test
- horizontalKnockbackDeduction divides rather than subtracts
- combo mode measures height against the attacker and replaces vertical
  motion, and enableVerticalLimit zeroes it once the victim floats too
  high

